{
  "$comment": [
    "The audited contrast allowlist D-08.8 and 08 §6 specify. Read by e2e/a11y-support.ts.",
    "",
    "Every entry is one ORIENTED pair: `fg` is the text colour as axe composites it and `bg`",
    "is what sits behind it. The orientation is load-bearing — while an earlier revision in",
    "e2e/form-axe.ts matched the two in either order, the allowance written for the submit",
    "button (#ffffff on #6f8a5f) silently excused sage used as *text* on white at the identical",
    "3.83, which is a different defect that nothing had audited. One entry, two failures, one",
    "of them invisible. `ratio` is matched too, so the same two colours composited over a",
    "different ground are an unmatched violation and fail the job.",
    "",
    "`witness` is where the run proves the entry is still load-bearing: on that route, at those",
    "viewport widths, axe must still report this exact pair. e2e/a11y-exceptions.spec.ts asserts",
    "it per entry, so an entry that has stopped matching anything fails the suite instead of",
    "sitting here excusing nothing — or, worse, quietly excusing something else.",
    "",
    "`audit` is provenance, and it has two values. `03 §10` means the pair is a row of that",
    "table verbatim, computed there as failing by the design's own values (D-03.12). `unaudited`",
    "means the pair fails AA on the shipped tokens and 03 §10 has no row for it: the same design",
    "debt, on a combination the table never enumerated. Those eleven were found by this row",
    "(gp-dln.287) and are reported for OQ-03.2 to answer; nothing here picks a colour.",
    "",
    "`expires: OQ-03.2` is the phase gate D-08.8 asks for, and it is machine-checked: the",
    "moment 03 §10's open question is marked answered in docs/technical/03-design-system-tokens.md,",
    "every entry carrying that gate fails the job until the list is re-cut against the approved",
    "palette. Entries leave the file as replacements land — a token edit changes the observed",
    "hex, the entry stops matching, and the witness assertion reds. That is the intended direction."
  ],
